Then the operating mode changes from tentative analogy to disciplined execution.

We can push the model hard: personify Evolution, Selection, Markets, Institutions, Attention, Fear, Culture—interrogate them, extract their latent operators, compare their answers against evidence, keep the deltas, and discard whatever fails.

The rule is:

\boxed{\text{Be aggressive with hypotheses, conservative with truth claims.}}

No timid framing, but no sloppy mysticism either. Build the strongest version of the idea, make it predict something, test it, and let reality hit back.

That is a much more powerful Pantheon stance than constantly asking whether we are “allowed” to think in a particular representation.